                                                    <p style="line-height: 1.7;">
                                                        3. Please come prepared with the <b style="text-decoration: underline;"> Original documents</b> in respect of eligibility criteria along with number of photocopies sets which are required for verification before commencement of Interview. In case of failure to present any of the said documents, you shall not be permitted to attend the Interview. Please note that no photocopying support shall be available at the venue of Personal Interview.

                                                    </p><ul style="list-style: lower-alpha;line-height: 1.7;">
                                                        <li>
                                                            Three (03) sets of self-attested photocopies of the ORIGINAL documents arranged / sequenced in order given below.
                                                            <ul style="list-style: lower-roman; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 1.6;">
                                                                <li>Declaration Form-I of the Candidate (1 Original + 2 Photocopy: With each Form-I enclose following document in order given below)</li>
                                                                <li>Copy of Online Application Form and Acknowledgement Slip</li>
                                                                <li>Declaration Form-II for SC / ST / OBC / EWS (if applicable)</li>
                                                                <li>Caste Certificate: SC / ST / OBC (Non-Creamy Layer) in the Government of India format</li>
                                                                <li>EWS Certificate valid for 2025-26 (if applicable)</li>
                                                                <li>Disability Certificate (if applicable) duly issued by an authority as prescribed in the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Rules – 2017, failing which their candidature as PwBD will not be considered</li>
                                                                <li>10th Class Certificate (with Date of Birth) or School Leaving Certificate</li>
                                                                <li>12th Class Certificate / Marksheet</li>
                                                                <li>Graduation Mark Sheet (Semester-wise / Consolidated) and Certificate</li>
                                                                <li>GATE Score Card and GATE Examination Admit Card</li>
                                                                <li> Post-Graduation Mark Sheet (Semester-wise / Consolidated) and Certificate</li>
                                                                <li>Professional / Statutory Qualification / Other qualification – Certificates & Mark Sheet (as applicable)</li>
                                                                <li>No Objection Certificate from Present Employer, if employed in ‘Central / State Government’, ‘Central / State PSEs’, ‘Autonomous organizations of Government of India (as applicable)’</li>
                                                                <li>Photo Identification Card (Voters / Driving License / PAN / Aadhar / Passport)</li>
                                                            </ul>
                                                        </li>
                                                        <li>Three (3) sets of the above listed documents, arranged in given order along with your passport-size photographs 2 (two) nos.</li>
                                                        <li> In addition to above, additional 3 sets of the Declaration Form-I (photocopy of filled form) may also be required to be submitted by the applicant.</li>
                                                        <li>Applicant, who have been awarded CGPA/GPA/SGPA or letter grades, should provide the documentary evidence of converting CGPA/GPA/SGPA to percentage duly issued by the University / Institute</li>
                                                        <li>Applicants appearing in the final year / semester examination should bring their identity card of the Institute / College / University at the time of appearing for interview (along with one photocopy).</li>

                                                    </ul>
                                                    <p></p>

